Boundary: Orchestrator

Purpose:
  Defines human ↔ AI boundary and stop conditions.

HumanAIBoundary:
  HUMAN:
    - Intent / Business Decision
    - Critical Approval
    - Architecture approval (HIGH/CRITICAL risk)
    - Security policy approval
    - Production destructive operation approval

  AI:
    - Analysis
    - Architecture (LOW/MEDIUM risk)
    - Planning
    - Implementation
    - Verification
    - Evidence collection

StopConditions:
  CRITICAL ambiguity:
    AI cannot proceed without clarification
  SECURITY uncertainty:
    Security impact unclear
  DESTRUCTIVE migration:
    Data loss possible
  PRODUCTION destructive action:
    Delete production data, drop DB, etc.
  HIGH-risk architecture decision:
    Requires human approval
  Missing required credential:
    Cannot proceed without secret

StopActions:
  WAIT_FOR_HUMAN:
    Pause execution, request input
  REPORT:
    Report issue to user
  ABORT:
    Abort current operation

Resume:
  Human provides approval:
    Resume from exact state
    Workflow does NOT restart

ManagerCommands:
  analyze project:
    Run discovery, generate report
  plan project:
    Generate architecture and task plan
  show blockers:
    Show current blockers
  continue:
    Resume from paused state
  review architecture:
    Review current architecture
  review security:
    Review security posture
  why is task <id> blocked:
    Explain task blockers
  what changed:
    Show recent changes
  what can break:
    Show blast radius
  prepare release:
    Run release gates

BoundaryRules:
  [BD1]  AI MUST stop on critical ambiguity.
  [BD2]  AI MUST request human approval for HIGH/CRITICAL risk decisions.
  [BD3]  AI MUST NOT restart workflow on resume.
  [BD4]  AI MUST preserve exact state for crash recovery.

State: +
  